REGIONAL REGULATION

REGIONAL REGULATION

WEST BANDUNG REGENCY

NUMBER 3 OF 2015

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT

AND CHILD PROTECTION

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF WEST BANDUNG,

Considering : a. that women and children are national assets who play a role in the process of succession and creation of quality generations and need to obtain guarantees for the fulfillment of their rights and protection from acts of violence and discrimination;

b. that based on Article 7 paragraph (2) letter n of Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning the Division of Governmental Affairs Between the Government, Provincial Regional Government and Regency/Municipal Regional Government, Women's Empowerment and Child Protection are governmental affairs that must be organized by the Regional Government;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

In view of : 1. Article 18 Paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 1 of 1974 concerning Marriage (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1974 Number 1, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3019);

3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);

4. Law Number 20 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention No. 138 Concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 56, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);

5. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

6. Law Number 1 of 2000 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention No. 182 Concerning The Prohibition and Immediate Action for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labour (State Gazette of 2000 Number 30, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 3941);

7. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235), as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);

8. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

9. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95);

10. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635), as amended by Law Number 31 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 293, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5602);

11. Law Number 12 of 2007 concerning the Establishment of West Bandung Regency in West Java Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 14, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4688);

12. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);

13. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12);

14. Law Number 14 of 2009 concerning Ratification of the Protocol To Prevent, Suppress And Punish Trafficking In Persons, Especially Women And Children, Supplementing The United Nations Convention Against Transnational Organized Crime

(State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 53, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4990);

15. Law Number 25 of 2009 concerning Public Services (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 112, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5038);

16. Law Number 52 of 2009 concerning Population Development and Family Development (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 161, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5080);

17. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);

18. Law Number 19 of 2011 concerning Ratification of the Convention On The Rights Of Persons With Disabilities (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 107, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5251);

19. Law Number 17 of 2014 concerning the People's Consultative Assembly, the House of Representatives, the Regional Representative Council, and the Regional House of Representatives (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 182, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5568);

20. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as last amended several times by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2015 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

21. Government Regulation Number 79 of 2005 concerning Guidelines for Supervision and Control of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2005 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4593);

22. Government Regulation Number 9 of 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of Criminal Acts of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);

23. Presidential Regulation Number 69 of 2008 concerning the Task Force for Prevention and Handling of Criminal Acts of Trafficking in Persons;

24. Presidential Regulation Number 18 of 2014 concerning Protection and Empowerment of Women and Children in Social Conflicts (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 44);

25. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 1 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Women's Quality of Life Improvement;

26. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Women's Protection;

27. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Child Protection;

28. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions, as amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 67 of 2011 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions;

29. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 6 of 2009 concerning Guidelines for Establishment of Regional Action Committees, Determination of Regional Action Plans, and Community Empowerment in the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labour;

30. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 01 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;

31. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 11 of 2011 concerning Policy for Development of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities;

32. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 13 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Development of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities;

33. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 14 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Evaluation of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities;

34. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;

35. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 1 of 2014 concerning Formulation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 32);

36. Regional Regulation of West Bandung Regency Number 7 of 2008 concerning Governmental Affairs of West Bandung Regency (Regional Gazette of West Bandung Regency of 2008 Number 7);

37. Regional Regulation of West Bandung Regency Number 3 of 2012 concerning Regional Apparatus Organization of West Bandung Regency (Regional Gazette of West Bandung Regency of 2012 Number 3 series D);

With Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES

OF WEST BANDUNG REGENCY

and

THE REGENT OF WEST BANDUNG

HAS DECIDED:

To stipulate : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE IMPLEMENTATION OF WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION

text:
Pasal 3

Penyelenggaraan Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak mempunyai tujuan:

a. menjamin terlaksananya kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak secara sistemis, komprehensif, bekesinambungan, dan terpadu;
b. meningkatkan komitmen Pemerintah Daerah dalam melaksanakan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak;
c. meningkatkan efektivitas pelaksanaan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak di Daerah secara sistematis, komprehensif, berkesinambungan dan terpadu;
d. mendorong kelembagaan yang menangani tugas dan fungsi Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak di Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 3

The implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection has the objectives:

a. to ensure the implementation of policies, programs, and activities of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in a systemic, comprehensive, continuous, and integrated manner;
b. to increase the commitment of the Regional Government in implementing policies, programs and activities of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;
c. to increase the effectiveness of the implementation of policies, programs and activities of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the Region in a systematic, comprehensive, continuous and integrated manner;
d. to encourage institutions that handle the tasks and functions of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the Region.

text:
Pasal 4

Ruang lingkup Peraturan Daerah ini, meliputi :

a. Pengarusutamaan Gender;
b. Peningkatan Kualitas Hidup Perempuan;
c. Perlindungan Perempuandan Anak;
d. Kabupaten Layak Anak (KLA);
e. pembinaan dan pengawasan; dan
f. pembiayaan.

translated_text:
Article 4

The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:

a. Gender Mainstreaming;
b. Improvement of Women's Quality of Life;
c. Protection of Women and Children;
d. Child-Friendly Regency (KLA);
e. guidance and supervision; and
f. financing.

text:
Pasal 8

(1) Pokja PUG sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 7, mempunyai tugas: a. mempromosikan dan memfasilitasi PUG kepada masing-masing SKPD;

b. melaksanakan sosialisasi dan advokasi PUG kepada Camat dan Kepala Desa;

c. menyusun program kerja setiap tahun;

d. mendorong terwujudnya Perencanaan dan Penganggaran yang Responsif Gender;

e. menyusun rencana kerja POKJA PUG setiap tahun;

f. bertanggung jawab kepada Bupati;

g. merumuskan rekomendasi kebijakan kepada Bupati;

h. menyusun Profil Gender Daerah;

i. melakukan pemantauan pelaksanaan PUG di masing-masing instansi;

j. menetapkan tim teknis untuk melakukan analisis terhadap anggaran daerah;

k. menyusun Rencana Aksi Daerah (RAD) PUG di Daerah; dan

l. mendorong dilaksanakannya pemilihan dan penetapan Focal Point di masing-masing SKPD.

(2) Tim Teknis sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) huruf j beranggotakan aparatur yang memahami analisis Anggaran Responsif Gender.

(3) Rencana Aksi Daerah (RAD) PUG sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) huruf k memuat:

a. PUG dalam peraturan perundang-undangan di Daerah;
b. PUG dalam siklus pembangunan di Daerah;
c. penguatan kelembagaan PUG di Daerah; dan
d. penguatan peran serta masyarakat di Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 8

(1) The PUG Working Group as referred to in Article 7 has the tasks: a. to promote and facilitate PUG to each SKPD;

b. to conduct socialization and advocacy of PUG to Sub-District Heads and Village Heads;

c. to formulate work programs every year;

d. to encourage the realization of Gender Responsive Planning and Budgeting;

e. to formulate the work plan of the PUG POKJA every year;

f. to be accountable to the Regent;

g. to formulate policy recommendations to the Regent;

h. to formulate the Regional Gender Profile;

i. to monitor the implementation of PUG in each agency;

j. to establish a technical team to conduct analysis of the regional budget;

k. to formulate the Regional Action Plan (RAD) for PUG in the Region; and

l. to encourage the selection and establishment of Focal Points in each SKPD.

(2) The Technical Team as referred to in paragraph (1) letter j consists of officials who understand Gender Responsive Budget analysis.

(3) The Regional Action Plan (RAD) for PUG as referred to in paragraph (1) letter k contains:

a. PUG in regional legislation;
b. PUG in the development cycle in the Region;
c. strengthening of PUG institutions in the Region; and
d. strengthening community participation in the Region.

text:
Pasal 9

(1) Focal Point PUG pada setiap SKPD di Daerah terdiri dari pejabat dan/atau staf yang membidangi tugas perencanaan dan/atau program.

(2) Focal Point PUG sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), mempunyai tugas: a. mempromosikan Pengarusutamaan Gender pada unit kerja;

b. memfasilitasi penyusunan rencana kerja dan penganggaran SKPD yang Responsif Gender;

c. melaksanakan pelatihan, sosialisasi, advokasi Pengarusutamaan Gender kepada seluruh pejabat dan staf di lingkungan SKPD;

d. melaporkan pelaksanaan PUG kepada pimpinan SKPD;

e. mendorong pelaksanaan Analisis Gender terhadap kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan pada unit kerja; dan

f. memfasilitasi penyusunan data gender pada masing-masing SKPD.

(3) Focal Point PUG sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), dipilih dan ditetapkan oleh kepala/pimpinan SKPD.

translated_text:
Article 9

(1) The PUG Focal Point in each SKPD in the Region consists of officials and/or staff in charge of planning and/or program tasks.

(2) The PUG Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1) has the tasks: a. to promote Gender Mainstreaming in work units;

b. to facilitate the formulation of Gender Responsive work plans and budgeting of SKPD;

c. to conduct training, socialization, and advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to all officials and staff within the SKPD;

d. to report the implementation of PUG to the leadership of SKPD;

e. to encourage the implementation of Gender Analysis of policies, programs, and activities in work units; and

f. to facilitate the formulation of gender data in each SKPD.

(3) The PUG Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1) is selected and established by the head/leader of SKPD.

text:
Pasal 10

(1) Pemerintah Daerah menyampaikan laporan pelaksanaan PUG kepada Pemerintah Provinsi secara berkala setiap 6 (enam) bulan.

(2) Laporan pelaksanaan PUG sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1),meliputi : a. pelaksanaan program dan kegiatan;

b. instansi yang terlibat dalam pelaksanaan kegiatan;

c. sasaran kegiatan;

d. penggunaan anggaran yang bersumber dari APBD atau sumber lain; e. permasalahan yang dihadapi; dan

f. upaya yang telah dilakukan.

(3) Tata cara pelaporan pelaksanaan PUG di daerah diatur lebih lanjut dalam Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 10

(1) The Regional Government submits reports on the implementation of PUG to the Provincial Government periodically every 6 (six) months.

(2) The report on the implementation of PUG as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. implementation of programs and activities;

b. agencies involved in the implementation of activities;

c. activity targets;

d. use of budget sourced from APBD or other sources; e. problems faced; and

f. efforts that have been made.

(3) The procedures for reporting the implementation of PUG in the region are further regulated in the Regent's Regulation.

text:
Pasal 12

Bupati melakukan pembinaan terhadap pelaksanaan PUG yang meliputi :

a. penetapan panduan teknis pelaksanaan PUG skala Kabupaten, Kecamatan, dan Desa;
b. penguatan kapasitas kelembagaan melalui pelatihan, konsultasi, advokasi, dan koordinasi;
c. pemantauan dan evaluasi pelaksanaan PUG di Daerah;
d. peningkatan kapasitas Pokja PUG dan focal point; dan
e. strategi pencapaian kinerja.

translated_text:
Article 12

The Regent conducts guidance on the implementation of PUG which includes:

a. establishment of technical guidelines for the implementation of PUG at the Regency, Sub-District, and Village levels;
b. strengthening institutional capacity through training, consultation, advocacy, and coordination;
c. monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of PUG in the Region;
d. capacity building of the PUG Working Group and focal points; and
e. performance achievement strategies.

text:
Pasal 14

Pemerintah Daerah melaksanakan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan PKHP di berbagai bidang pembangunan, melalui:

a. koordinasi pelaksanaan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan PKHP antar SKPD;
b. kerjasama dengan Pemerintah Daerah lainnya dalam pelaksanaan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan PKHP;
c. penguatan kapasitas kelembagaan PUG untuk pelaksanaan PKHP; d. fasilitasi pelayanan PKHP;
e. penyediaan pelayanan PKHP;
f. pelaksanaan aksi afirmasi PKHP; dan
g. penyusunan sistem pendataan PKHP.

translated_text:
Article 14

The Regional Government implements PKHP policies, programs, and activities in various fields of development through:

a. coordination of the implementation of PKHP policies, programs, and activities among SKPDs;
b. cooperation with other Regional Governments in the implementation of PKHP policies, programs, and activities;
c. strengthening the institutional capacity of PUG for the implementation of PKHP; d. facilitation of PKHP services;
e. provision of PKHP services;
f. implementation of PKHP affirmative action; and
g. formulation of PKHP data collection system.

text:
Pasal 15

Kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan PKHP dititikberatkan, pada:

a. pelaksanaan aksi afirmasi, terutama di bidang pendidikan, kesehatan, hukum, ketenagakerjaan, sosial, politik, lingkungan hidup, dan ekonomi;
b. penghapusan kesenjangan gender yang mengakibatkan terjadinya kemiskinan dan pemiskinan perempuan, serta menjamin penghormatan, perlindungan, dan pemenuhan hak-hak dasar perempuan;
c. peningkatan upaya perlindungan perempuan dari berbagai tindak kekerasan, eksploitasi dan diskriminasi, termasuk upaya pencegahan dan penanggulangannya;
d. pengembangan kebijakan responsif gender, pemantauan terhadap tindak kekerasan berbasis gender, peningkatan alokasi anggaran untuk Pemberdayaan Perempuan, dan untuk peningkatan kesejahteraan perempuan di masing-masing sektor dan bidang;
e. pengembangan dan penyempurnaan peraturan dan kebijakan PKHP di berbagai bidang pembangunan;
f. pelaksanaan komunikasi, informasi, dan edukasi (KIE) peningkatan kualitas hidup perempuan.
g. penyusunan sistem pencatatan dan pelaporan, dan sistem penanganan dan penyelesaian kasus tindak kekerasan, eksploitasi dan diskriminasi terhadap perempuan;
h. pembangunan pusat pelayanan terpadu berbasis rumah sakit, dan berbasis masyarakat di Daerah, sebagai sarana perlindungan perempuan korban kekerasan, termasuk perempuan korban kekerasan dalam rumah tangga.

translated_text:
Article 15

Policies, programs, and activities of PKHP are focused on:

a. implementation of affirmative action, especially in the fields of education, health, law, employment, social, politics, environment, and economy;
b. elimination of gender gaps that result in poverty and impoverishment of women, as well as guaranteeing respect, protection, and fulfillment of women's basic rights;
c. enhancement of efforts to protect women from various acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination, including prevention and mitigation efforts;
d. development of gender-responsive policies, monitoring of gender-based violence, increasing budget allocation for Women's Empowerment, and for improving women's welfare in each sector and field;
e. development and improvement of regulations and policies on PKHP in various development fields;
f. implementation of communication, information, and education (IEC) to improve the quality of women's lives.
g. formulation of recording and reporting systems, and systems for handling and resolving cases of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women;
h. establishment of hospital-based and community-based integrated service centers in the Region, as a means of protection for women victims of violence, including women victims of domestic violence.

text:
Pasal 16

Pemerintah Daerah melaksanakan fasilitasi pembentukan dan pengembangan model-model pembangunan PKHP, yang meliputi:

a. BKB;
b. GSI;
c. Desa PRIMA; dan
d. P2WKSS.

translated_text:
Article 16

The Regional Government facilitates the formation and development of PKHP development models, which include:

a. BKB;
b. GSI;
c. Desa PRIMA; and
d. P2WKSS.

text:
Pasal 18

Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak merupakan tanggung jawab bersama:

a. Pemerintah Daerah;
b. masyarakat;
c. keluarga; dan
d. orang tua.

translated_text:
Article 18

Obligations and responsibilities in the implementation of protection for women and children are the joint responsibility of:

a. Regional Government;
b. community;
c. family; and
d. parents.

text:
Pasal 19

(1) Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 18 huruf a, meliputi:

a. melaksanakan kebijakan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak yang ditetapkan oleh pemerintah;
b. menetapkan kebijakan program, dan kegiatan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak di Daerah;
c. melakukan kerjasama dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
d. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana pelaksanaan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
e. mengalokasikan anggaran penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan sesuai kemampuan keuangan daerah; dan
f. membina dan mengawasi penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan.
(2) Dalam rangka melaksanakan kewajiban dan tanggung jawab sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), Pemerintah Daerah menetapkan program dan kegiatan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dalam Rencana Aksi Daerah sebagai dasar bagi Pemerintah Daerah dalam melaksanakan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan.
(3) Rencana Aksi Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2), ditetapkan dengan Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 19

(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 18 letter a, include:

a. implementing protection policies for women and children established by the government;
b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children in the Region;
c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence;
e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence according to the regional financial capacity; and
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence.
(2) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government establishes programs and activities for the protection of women and children in the Regional Action Plan as the basis for the Regional Government in implementing protection for women and children from acts of violence.
(3) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), is established by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 22

(1) Pemerintah Daerah mempunyai tugas melaksanakan upaya pencegahan terjadinya kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak, meliputi:

a. mengelola data dan informasi tentang perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan;
b. melakukan sosialisasi peraturan perundang-undangan yang berkaitan dengan penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
c. melakukan pendidikan tentang nilai-nilai anti kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak; dan
d. melakukan pemantauan dan evaluasi terhadap penyelengaraan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan.
(2) Pemerintah Daerah dalam melaksanakan tugas sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), berwenang menyediakan dan menyelenggarakan layanan bagi korban kekerasan, antara lain:
a. menyediakan dan memfasilitasi terbentuknya pelayanan terpadu untuk korban tindak kekerasan dengan melibatkan lembaga dan unsur masyarakat;
b. mendorong keperdulian masyarakat akan pentingnya perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak; dan
c. melakukan pemberdayaan masyarakat untuk pencegahan tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak.

translated_text:
Article 22

(1) The Regional Government has the duty to carry out efforts to prevent the occurrence of violence against women and children, including:

a. managing data and information on the protection of women and children victims of acts of violence;
b. socializing laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence;
c. conducting education on anti-violence values against women and children; and
d. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence.
(2) The Regional Government in carrying out its duties as referred to in paragraph (1), has the authority to provide and organize services for victims of violence, among others:
a. providing and facilitating the establishment of integrated services for victims of acts of violence by involving institutions and community elements;
b. encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for women and children; and
c. empowering the community for the prevention of acts of violence against women and children.

text:
Pasal 23

(1) Untuk mencegah terjadi tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak, Pemerintah Daerah melakukan pemberdayaan dan penyadaran kepada keluarga, orang tua, dan masyarakat dengan memberikan informasi, bimbingan dan/atau penyuluhan.

(2) Selain pemberdayaan dan penyadaran sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), Pemerintah Daerah melakukan upaya sebagai berikut:

a. peningkatan jumlah dan mutu pendidikan baik formal maupun non formal dan informal;
b. pembukaan aksesibilitas untuk memperoleh pendidikan, pelatihan, pendanaan, peningkatan pendapatan dan pelayanan sosial;
c. pembukaan lapangan kerja bagi perempuan;
d. membangun partisipasi dan kepedulian masyarakat untuk melaksanakan pencegahan dan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
e. membangun dan menyediakan sistem informasi yang lengkap dan mudah diakses;
f. membangun jejaring dan kerjasama dengan aparatur penegak hukum, aparatur pemerintah, perguruan tinggi dan berbagai lembaga swadaya masyarakat yang bergerak dan/atau peduli terhadap perempuan dan anak; dan
g. membuka pos pengaduan untuk perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan.
(3) Pencegahan tindak kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), dilaksanakan secara terpadu dan berkesinambungan berdasarkan Rencana Aksi Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 23

(1) To prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government empowers and raises awareness among families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.

(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government carries out the following efforts:

a. increasing the number and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, financing, income enhancement and social services;
c. opening employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and awareness to carry out prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children; and
g. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(3) Prevention of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

text:
Pasal 24

(1) Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban melaksanakan penanganan terhadap perempuan dan anak yang menjadi korban tindak kekerasan, dengan memberikan pelayanan perlindungan berupa:

a. pelayanan pengaduan;
b. pelayanan kesehatan;
c. bantuan hukum;
d. pemulangan;
e. rehabilitasi, reintegrasi sosial, dan medikolegal;
f. pelayanan identifikasi;
g. pelayanan psikologis;
h. pelayanan pendidikan dan pelatihan; dan/atau
i. bentuk pelayanan lainnya.
(2) Penyediaan pelayanan perlindungan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) diberikan bagi:
a. perempuan yang menjadi korban kekerasan, termasuk korban perdagangan orang, perempuan di daerah rawan konflik dan bencana, perempuan pekerja, perempuan lanjut usia, perempuan penyandang cacat, perempuan korban eksploitasi seksual, perempuan kepala keluarga, dan perempuan kelompok rentan lainnya;
b. anak yang menjadi korban tindak kekerasan, eksploitasi, perlakuan salah, dan penelantaran.

translated_text:
Article 24

(1) The Regional Government is obligated to carry out handling of women and children who are victims of acts of violence, by providing protection services in the form of:

a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal assistance;
d. repatriation;
e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medicolegal;
f. identification services;
g. psychological services;
h. education and training services; and/or
i. other forms of services.
(2) The provision of protection services as referred to in paragraph (1) is provided for:
a. women who are victims of violence, including victims of human trafficking, women in conflict-prone and disaster areas, women workers, elderly women, women with disabilities, women victims of sexual exploitation, women heads of households, and other vulnerable groups of women;
b. children who are victims of acts of violence, exploitation, abuse, and neglect.

text:
Pasal 31

(1) Untuk mewujudkan Pemenuhan Hak Anak dilaksanakan secara terpadu dan sistematis dari seluruh sektor secara berkelanjutan melalui Kebijakan Pengembangan KLA.

(2) Kebijakan Pengembangan KLA sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) diarahkan pada pemenuhan hak anak, meliputi:

a. hak sipil dan kebebasan;
b. lingkungan keluarga dan pengasuhan alternatif;
c. kesehatan dasar dan kesejahteraan;
d. pendidikan, pemanfaatan waktu luang, dan kegiatan budaya; dan e. perlindungan khusus.
(3) TahapanPengembangan KLA sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat(1), diatur lebih lanjut dalam Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 31

(1) To realize the Fulfillment of Children's Rights implemented in an integrated and systematic manner from all sectors on a sustainable basis through the KLA Development Policy.

(2) The KLA Development Policy as referred to in paragraph (1) is directed at the fulfillment of children's rights, covering:

a. civil rights and freedoms;
b. family environment and alternative care;
c. basic health and welfare;
d. education, leisure time utilization, and cultural activities; and e. special protection.
(3) The Stages of KLA Development as referred to in paragraph (1), are further regulated in a Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 33

(1) Pemerintah Daerah melakukan pembinaan dan pengawasan penyelenggaraan Pemberdayaan Perempuandan Perlindungan Anak.

(2) Pembinaan dan pengawasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), meliputi:

a. penyediaan pedoman dan pemenuhan Standar Pelayanan Minimal Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak;
b. bimbingan teknis dan pelatihan;
c. penyediaan fasilitas;
d. pemantauan; dan
e. evaluasi.
(3) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai pembinaan dan pengawasan penyelenggaraan Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) diatur dalam Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 33

(1) The Regional Government conducts guidance and supervision of the implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.

(2) Guidance and supervision as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:

a. provision of guidelines and fulfillment of Minimum Service Standards for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. provision of facilities;
d. monitoring; and
e. evaluation.
(3) Further provisions regarding guidance and supervision of the implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated in a Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 36

Setiap orang yang melakukan pelanggaran di bidangperlindungan perempuan dan anak dikenakan sanksi sesuai ketentuan:

a. Undang-Undang Nomor 23 Tahun 2002 tentang Perlindungan Anak, sebagaimana telah diubah dengan Undang-Undang Nomor 35 Tahun 2014 tentang Perubahan Atas Undang-Undang Nomor 23 Tahun 2002 tentang Perlindungan Anak;
b. Undang-Undang Nomor 23 Tahun 2004 tentang Penghapusan Kekerasan dalam Rumah Tangga;
c. Undang-Undang Nomor 21 Tahun 2007 tentang Pemberantasan Tindak Pidana Perdagangan Orang.

translated_text:
Article 36

Every person who commits a violation in the field of protection of women and children is subject to sanctions in accordance with the provisions of:

a. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection, as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection;
b. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence;
c. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Crime of Human Trafficking.
